{"content":[{"c":["BETHANY"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Village on the eastern slope of the Mt of Olives about a mile and a half (2.4 kilometers) east of Jerusalem. Jesus and his disciples sometimes stayed in Bethany when in Judea, as when they attended temple observances during Passover (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.21.17","r":"Matt.21.17","rawR":"Matt.21.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.21.17","value":"Matt.21.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 21:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.11.11","r":"Mark.11.11","rawR":"Mark.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.11.11","value":"Mark.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 11:11"},"). Jesus was eating at the home of Simon the leper in Bethany when a woman came and anointed his head with costly perfume (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.26.6-13","r":"Matt.26.6-13","rawR":"Matt.26.6-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.26.6-13","value":"Matt.26.6-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 26:6-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.14.3-9","r":"Mark.14.3-9","rawR":"Mark.14.3-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.14.3-9","value":"Mark.14.3-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 14:3-9"},"). Bethany was also the home of Mary and Martha and their brother Lazarus, where Jesus raised Lazarus from the dead (",{"href":"?bref=John.11.1,18","r":"John.11.1,18","rawR":"John.11.1,18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.1,18","value":"John.11.1,18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:1, 18"},"). The village was near Bethphage on an approach to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.11.1","r":"Mark.11.1","rawR":"Mark.11.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.11.1","value":"Mark.11.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 11:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.19.29","r":"Luke.19.29","rawR":"Luke.19.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.19.29","value":"Luke.19.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 19:29"},") that Jesus followed in preparation for his triumphal entry into Jerusalem. In Bethany Jesus blessed his disciples after the resurrection and parted from them (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.24.50","r":"Luke.24.50","rawR":"Luke.24.50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.24.50","value":"Luke.24.50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 24:50"},"). Today the town is called el-Azariyeh (the place of Lazarus)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Village on “the other side of the Jordan” (the east side), where John the Baptist baptized (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.28","r":"John.1.28","rawR":"John.1.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.28","value":"John.1.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 1:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bethany","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mt 21:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.21.17","rawQueryValue":"Matt.21.17","sourceRefExact":"Matt.21.17"},{"anchorText":"Mk 11:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.11.11","rawQueryValue":"Mark.11.11","sourceRefExact":"Mark.11.11"},{"anchorText":"Mt 26:6-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.26.6-13","rawQueryValue":"Matt.26.6-13","sourceRefExact":"Matt.26.6-13"},{"anchorText":"Mk 14:3-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.14.3-9","rawQueryValue":"Mark.14.3-9","sourceRefExact":"Mark.14.3-9"},{"anchorText":"Jn 11:1, 18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.11.1,18","rawQueryValue":"John.11.1,18","sourceRefExact":"John.11.1,18"},{"anchorText":"Mk 11:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.11.1","rawQueryValue":"Mark.11.1","sourceRefExact":"Mark.11.1"},{"anchorText":"Lk 19:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.19.29","rawQueryValue":"Luke.19.29","sourceRefExact":"Luke.19.29"},{"anchorText":"Lk 24:50","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.24.50","rawQueryValue":"Luke.24.50","sourceRefExact":"Luke.24.50"},{"anchorText":"Jn 1:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.1.28","rawQueryValue":"John.1.28","sourceRefExact":"John.1.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1b7850af595e7b282656b2d0f903d7db58e9719ce78ec3d241bb1bb0e933d94f","sourceItemName":"Bethany","sourceItemOrder":227,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bethany","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bethany","title":"Bethany","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}